      "values": [
        [
          "PHRASAL (PITCH) ACCENT GROUPING — ANNOTATION INSTRUCTIONS"
        ],
        [
          ""
        ],
        [
          "STEP 1 — prescreening"
        ],
        [
          "  Annotate each element row in this tab."
        ],
        [
          "  When finished: mark 'prescreening' as 'ready-for-review' in the Status tab."
        ],
        [
          "  The coordinator will then regenerate the dependent tab."
        ],
        [
          ""
        ],
        [
          "STEP 2 — general"
        ],
        [
          "  This tab is generated after prescreening is imported."
        ],
        [
          "  Do NOT annotate it until the coordinator confirms regeneration is complete."
        ],
        [
          ""
        ],
        [
          "DETAILS"
        ],
        [
          ""
        ],
        [
          "STEP 1 — prescreening: For each element, annotate accented (same criterion metrical uses):"
        ],
        [
          "  y    = this element can always independently carry a phrasal pitch accent"
        ],
        [
          "  n    = this element can never independently carry a phrasal pitch accent;"
        ],
        [
          "         it will be EXCLUDED from the pair list in Step 2"
        ],
        [
          "  both = variably accent-bearing depending on context"
        ],
        [
          "When finished, mark prescreening as \"ready-for-review\" in the Status tab. The coordinator will then regenerate the general tab with a filtered pair list."
        ],
        [
          "STEP 2 — general: Do NOT annotate this tab until the coordinator confirms it has been regenerated after Step 1 is complete. Once regenerated, annotate each pair of linearly adjacent accent-eligible elements:"
        ],
        [
          "  joint_accent = always     one member obligatorily deaccents next to the other"
        ],
        [
          "  joint_accent = never      both always retain independent accents when adjacent"
        ],
        [
          "  joint_accent = sometimes  depends on focus/givenness/speech register"
        ],
        [
          "Corrective accent (e.g. \"HE did it, not SHE\") is out of scope — do not code pairs elicited or observed under a correction context (see issue #237 for the literature distinguishing corrective from contrastive/ordinary accent)."
        ]
